Quasar-authored. Issue #1663: a PyroWave stop could hang the agent forever on NVIDIA.

The pyrowaveenc element hands PyroWave the session's shared VkDevice (borrowed:
Granite's Context has owned_device = false). Granite still called vkDeviceWaitIdle
on it, in Device::wait_idle_nolock (device destroy, and init_frame_contexts at
create) holding only the one queue lock it is given, and again in
Context::destroy_device with no lock at all. vkDeviceWaitIdle needs every queue of
the device externally synchronised; the compositor and the Vulkan video encoder keep
submitting on that device while PyroWave is torn down, and NVIDIA 615.78.08 then
waited forever with the GPU idle.

On a borrowed device Granite now waits only for its own submissions: every one is
recorded in a frame (a per-queue timeline value, or a fence without timeline
semaphores), so waiting each frame covers all queues Granite submits to before it
frees anything. A frame now records a submit's timeline value only once
vkQueueSubmit2 succeeded: a failed submit signals nothing, and waiting for its value
would hang. Without timeline semaphores a failed fence submit still leaves its fence
in the frame (unchanged upstream behaviour); Quasar never takes that path, since its
device is Vulkan 1.3 with every supported feature enabled and timelineSemaphore is
required from 1.2.

Two assumptions this rests on:
- Context::destroy_device skips its wait because Device::~Device already waited; that
  holds only while the Device is destroyed before its Context (PyroWave's opaque
  device declares the Context first, pyrowave_c.cpp).
- Submits of a borrowed command buffer (submit_external) are not recorded in a frame;
  they are safe only because Quasar waits each on its own fence before returning
  (gst-pyrowave gpu.rs Shared::submit). Making that submit asynchronous needs this
  patch revisited.

The owned-device path is unchanged. Applied to Granite at GRANITE_REF by
deploy/Dockerfile.vulkan; re-apply on every PyroWave/Granite bump. One
vkDeviceWaitIdle stays reachable on a borrowed device: breadcrumbs.cpp
notify_device_hung, only with Granite post-mortem on (off in Quasar) after a hang.

